#ASSERT `Part 1 — the answer to` (`a claim for` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle` `of origin` `neither a natural disaster nor an accident` `, sudden` TRUE) `assessed as` (`the assessment: extent` (0%) `, value at the loss` 480_000_000 `, costs` 0 `and` 0 `, instructed` FALSE `, police concluded` FALSE `, wreck kept` FALSE `valued at` 0 `, other sums insured` EMPTY `, already paid` 0 `, earlier losses` 0 `, set off` FALSE)) `under` `the standard policy` EQUALS `not yet payable, because the police have not concluded the theft`
#ASSERT `the amount paid out on` (`a claim for` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle` `of origin` `neither a natural disaster nor an accident` `, sudden` TRUE) `assessed as` (`the assessment: extent` (0%) `, value at the loss` 480_000_000 `, costs` 0 `and` 0 `, instructed` FALSE `, police concluded` TRUE `, wreck kept` FALSE `valued at` 0 `, other sums insured` EMPTY `, already paid` 0 `, earlier losses` 0 `, set off` FALSE)) `under` (`the standard car insured for` 400_000_000 `of a value of` 500_000_000 `, deductible` (`a deductible per loss of` 1_000_000)) EQUALS 383_000_000

-- 13.3: replaced parts and a recovered stolen vehicle belong to UIC.
